Install Jenkins – Install Jenkins on your Linux server and access it on port 8080.

3. Install Plugins – Install Git, GitHub Integration, and Pipeline plugins.

4. Connect GitHub – Configure GitHub repository URL and credentials in Jenkins.

5. Configure Webhook – Add Jenkins webhook URL in GitHub settings to trigger builds automatically.

6. Create Jenkinsfile – Add pipeline stages:

Checkout – Download code from GitHub.

Build – Compile application.

Test – Execute test cases.

Package – Generate JAR/WAR file.

Deploy – Deploy application to the server.

7. Create Jenkins Pipeline – Configure Jenkins to use the Jenkinsfile from GitHub.

8. Push Code – Developer pushes updated code to GitHub.

9. Automatic Deployment – Jenkins automatically builds, tests, and deploys the application.
